### Steps to reproduce

This is a bit of a regression between pre-17.3 versions and new ones. I have extracted common `onExit` logic in a mixin that I apply to type-safe routes that need it. With the newer implementation of the builder such method is not detected and `hasOverridenOnExit` is set to `false` during generation and as a result the method is not triggered. 

From what I see this is because the check for the flag looks only at methods that are defined in the class itself
https://github.com/flutter/packages/blob/108dad0d562e9368a45b6b5cdcc26c137bc071c4/packages/go_router_builder/lib/src/route_config.dart#L707-L709

### Expected results

The `hasOverridenOnExit` to be set to `true` if an `onExit` method is present in a mixin and/or base class. 

### Actual results

The `hasOverridenOnExit` is set to `false` when `onExit` method is defined in a mixin

### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
@TypedGoRoute<ContactEditRoute>(path: '/contact/:id')
class ContactEditRoute extends GoRouteData with $ContactEditRoute, UnsavedChangesConfirmer {
  final int id;

  ContactEditRoute({required this.id});

  @override
  ChangeDetectionInterface buildChangeDetectionPage(BuildContext context, GoRouterState state) =>
      ContactEditPage(contactId: id);
}


mixin UnsavedChangesConfirmer on GoRouteData {
  static ChangeDetectionInterface? _currPage;

  ChangeDetectionInterface buildChangeDetectionPage(
      BuildContext context, GoRouterState state);

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context, GoRouterState state) {
    _currPage = buildChangeDetectionPage(context, state);

    return _currPage! as Widget;
  }

  @override
  FutureOr<bool> onExit(BuildContext context, GoRouterState state) async {
    if (_currPage?.hasChanges() == false) {
      return true;
    }

    final saveChanges = await showUnsavedChangesConfirm(context);

    if (saveChanges == null) {
      return false;
    }

    if (saveChanges == false) {
      return true;
    }

    return await _currPage!.performSave(isReloadIn: false);
  }
}
```

</details>


