### Actual results

The field keeps the focus in the framework, and its caret keeps blinking, but nothing typed after the click appears. `document.activeElement` is the `flutter-view` element.

Clicking a part of the tap region that has no semantics node, such as empty space in a `Container`, does not break typing.

What I think happens: the mouse press on the text's semantics element moves the browser focus to its nearest focusable ancestor, the `flutter-view` element. With semantics enabled, the field types into the `<input>` of its `SemanticTextField`, whose `blur` listener calls `SemanticsTextEditingStrategy.deactivate`. Nothing activates it again, because the framework focus never changed. With semantics disabled, the default editing strategy handles the same blur by focusing its `<input>` again.

Workaround: keep the browser from moving the focus.

```dart
// Called once at startup, on the web only.
web.EventStreamProviders.mouseDownEvent
    .forTarget(web.document, useCapture: true)
    .listen((event) {
  final active = web.document.activeElement;
  if (active?.getAttribute('data-semantics-role') != 'text-field') return;
  final target = event.target as web.Element;
  if (target.getAttribute('data-semantics-role') == 'text-field') return;
  if (target.closest('flt-semantics') != null) event.preventDefault();
});
```

